<title>USA: Texaco CEO sees WTI at $19.50/bbl '97 avg.</title>
<headline>Texaco CEO sees WTI at $19.50/bbl '97 avg.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc's chief executive Peter Bijur said his company expects West Texas Intermediate crude prices to average $19.50 a barrel in 1997, up $1.50 from Texaco's 1996 estimate.</p>
<p>&quot;While these figures may seem conservative to some, they seem very appropriate to us,&quot; Bijur told executives attending the company's annual analyst meeting at its headquarters.</p>
<p>Bijur added that upstream growth will prove to be a major component of the company's future expenditures.</p>
<p>-- Matt Daily, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
